Hi, Bob.

I'm on the launch-pad from JILA - leaving in a few minutes, then travelling
for 2 weeks and back in Durham on 7 Sept. I don't expect to have much email
contact until I'm in Durham.

I've tried to put the new dspotfit on scienide, but haven't been able to
connect; trying telnet just now, I see that ftp is disabled because of
attempted break-ins. So you'll have to pick up the files from me instead of
vice versa. And do it soon, in case JILA removes my account.

Do ftp to jilau1.colorado.edu, and use account jmh, password ebm12ece The
files are in directory dspotfit; have a look at Makefile to see which .f
files are actually needed.

This version implements the new ofrm of the potential that we discussed (as
in betaTRIAL) and implements fitting to vD with IETP = 'VD' instead of 'BV',
'FS' etc. The new calculations are done in dvddp and scatln. You need to set
J=0 for the scattering length calculation to work. For a sample channel 4
data file (for K2), look in fort.4 in the same directory.

Good luck!

Jeremy
